# Secure Auth Core

Stack: Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Supabase Auth, `@supabase/ssr`, Tailwind CSS.

## Before writing code

Always explain the security decision first (threat, control, why), then implement.

## Non-negotiables

- Prefer Server Components; use `"use client"` only for interactivity (forms, listeners).
- Never use `service_role` in Client Components or any browser-exposed code.
- Store Supabase session in cookies via `@supabase/ssr` (not localStorage-only auth).
- Protect private routes in `middleware.ts` (session check + redirect).
- Validate and sanitize inputs before calling Supabase Auth.
- Map auth/DB errors to generic user messages; log details server-side only.
- User-owned tables must include `user_id` and enforce Row Level Security (RLS).

## Env keys

- Client / browser: `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` only.
- `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`: server-only, never import into client bundles.
